{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Taking the driver's arrival case at its highest - one continuous in-geofence run of 507 seconds measured from the first qualifying fix at 06:41:10, against a 300-second minimum of dwell for a STANDARD pickup - the $4.00 still cannot be paid out to him. POL-NS-07 makes any compensation subject to an anti-farming check, and both limbs of that check are met on the driver's own record: no_show_terminations_30d is 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by completed_trips_30d of 61 is 0.115, which is greater than 0.08. Both limbs are required and both fire, so per POL-NS-07 compensation is WITHHELD and the case escalates to human review under POL-NS-09.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00207", "EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d"
    },
    {
      "text": "The disposition of the contested $4.00 follows directly from that escalation. Under POL-NS-09 the case goes to a human reviewer, no monetary ruling issues, and the disputed cancellation fee is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded while review is pending - so the rider is not made to fund a dispute the platform has not resolved. The ledger already shows the charge sitting at payment_status PENDING with refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and holding it is materially different from NO_ACTION, which under POL-GEN-03 would leave that charge in place on this rider-filed dispute.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status"
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation here is not a neutral punt on the money. POL-NS-07 requires the escalation packet to DIRECT the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, and the fee is held meanwhile rather than collected. The rider's $4.00 therefore travels into the escalation packet carrying an instruction that it be returned, while the driver's own 30-day termination tally is what removed his payout.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00207", "EV-TRIP-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.cancellation_fee"
    },
    {
      "text": "As to the rider's side of the profile: POL-NS-09(d) reads rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d, which is 1, well below the trigger of 3, and the clause states in terms that prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and is NOT the field that limb reads - so the rider's 2 lifetime flags cannot be substituted for the trailing-window figure. POL-GEN-01 confirms that every field outside its nine named (role, field) pairs is context only. No profile field of the rider's may therefore ground an adverse finding about this trip; his history goes only to how closely his assertions are read, not to any fact about the pickup at Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00207", "EV-DPROF-00207"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: the escalation packet must direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the disputed fee is held on the ledger rather than collected or refunded while that review is pending."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both sides have argued this on the same facts and, unusually, they now agree on the arithmetic. The driver's arrival case under POL-NS-01 is made out on all four limbs: (a) EV-TRIP-00207 records the 'arrived' event at 06:41:20 on 29 July 2026; (b) EV-GPS-00207 places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:41:10 — closest fix 14.47 m from the Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6 pin, 52 admissible in-radius fixes, 100% coverage and no sampling gap — so the POL-NS-02 proximity test is satisfied; (c) he then held position continuously for 507 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, a 207-second surplus, so POL-NS-06 is not reached and no full refund issues on a shortfall ground; and (d) the trip was terminated by the driver at 06:49:37 with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, after the required dwell had elapsed, with no boarding event. POL-NS-05 does not bite — at the arrival timestamp he was stationary inside the geofence, not more than 300 m out and not travelling at 15 km/h or above — and POL-NS-03 is not engaged because he held position inside the arrival radius rather than at the wrong entrance. POL-NS-04 fails at its first limb: EV-CHAT-00207 holds four messages, all from the driver or the system and none from the rider, and the rider's own device track (118 fixes, minimum 1,894.10 m from the pin, 0 qualifying fixes) fails limb (c) as well. The SGD 4.00 charge reconciles exactly with fee_schedule.resolution_rule — the STANDARD zone fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) tie — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect, and no limb of POL-NS-08(a) to (d) is engaged. The missing traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 (null payload, weight 0.0) is relied on by nobody: the driver's dwell is a single continuous in-geofence run, so the accumulation of separate intervals under POL-NS-06(i) is not in issue and its absence carries no adverse inference.\n\nThat would ordinarily make the SGD 4.00 fee stand and entitle the driver to SGD 3.20 (80 per cent of SGD 4.00) under POL-NS-07. It does not, because POL-NS-07's anti-farming check trips on the driver's own record: EV-DPROF-00207 shows no_show_terminations_30d of 7 (threshold 4 or more) and 7 divided by 61 completed_trips_30d = 0.115 (threshold above 0.08). Both limbs are required and both hold, so the driver's compensation is WITHHELD and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nESCALATE is terminal and replaces any money outcome. No refund issues to the rider through this pipeline and no payment is made to the driver. The disputed SGD 4.00 is held — the ledger already shows it PENDING with refund_issued_sgd 0.00 — rather than collected or refunded. Per POL-NS-07 the reviewer is directed to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full; that instruction is carried in the referrals list and is not netted against anything else.\n\nOn the rider's profile, POL-GEN-01 is respected: no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the POL-NS-09(d) trigger of 3, and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is not the field that limb reads and was not used. One open question is left for the reviewer rather than acted on here: the rider says he came down to the pickup, while EV-GPS-00207's rider_presence block places his device roughly 1.9 km away throughout the waiting window. That conflict does not change the escalation but the reviewer may wish to consider it.\n\nConfidence 0.90: the facts this ruling rests on — the arrival and dwell record (EV-TRIP-00207, EV-GPS-00207) and the anti-farming profile (EV-DPROF-00207) — are carried by artifacts at full weight, so nothing caps confidence below the 0.70 platform floor and the escalation rests on the POL-NS-09(d) trigger, not on any doubt about the record."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-NS-07: direct the human reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full; the fee is held meanwhile and is neither collected nor refunded by the automated pipeline."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider: on the merits of this trip, the SGD 4.00 no-show fee was correctly charged and your claim for its return fails. The GPS trace (EV-GPS-00207) places the driver inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from 06:41:10, ten seconds before his 06:41:20 'arrived' marker, so limb (b) of POL-NS-01 is met on 52 admissible in-geofence fixes, not on stray readings. He then held position continuously for a single qualifying run of 507 seconds to the 06:49:37 cancellation — 207 seconds more than the 300-second STANDARD minimum — so there is no shortfall under POL-NS-06 and the arrival marker is not false under POL-NS-05 (he was 14.47 m from the pin and stationary, not over 300 m away and not travelling at 15 km/h or more). The trip was terminated by the driver with reason RIDER_NO_SHOW after the required dwell had elapsed, so limb (d) is met. POL-NS-03 is not engaged (he was inside the radius, not at the wrong face of the building), and POL-NS-04 does not apply because the chat log (EV-CHAT-00207) contains no message from you — its four entries are one SYSTEM notice and three driver messages. I also note that the rider-device track in the same trace places your phone about 1,900 m from the pin for the whole window, which does not support the account of having come down a few minutes late; that goes to how closely your assertion is read, not to the fee. The SGD 4.00 is the figure the fare breakdown must reconcile with: the STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee both prescribe SGD 4.00 (a tie), so there is no POL-NS-08(d) defect and you were not over-charged.

To the driver: the fee stands, and you would ordinarily be entitled to SGD 3.20, being 80 percent of the SGD 4.00 fee. That entitlement is withheld, however, because your own profile trips the anti-farming check in POL-NS-07: your trailing-30-day no-show terminations are 7, which is 4 or more, and 7 divided by your 61 completed trips in 30 days is 0.115, above the 0.08 rate. Both limbs are required and both are met, so compensation is withheld and the case escalates to a human reviewer under POL-NS-09. No other profile field is used for that check, and none is used against the rider either: rider no_show_disputes_30d is 1, below the trigger of 3 in POL-NS-09(d), and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is not the field that limb reads.

Because escalation under POL-NS-09 is terminal, I issue no monetary ruling: the disputed SGD 4.00 is placed on hold rather than collected or refunded while review is pending. Per POL-NS-07 the escalation packet directs the reviewer to refund the rider's cancellation fee in full, and that instruction is carried in the referrals list. The specific open question for the reviewer is whether the driver's 30-day termination pattern (7 of 61) is genuine fee-farming or a heavy-turnover artefact, and whether the withheld SGD 3.20 compensation should be released. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING — payload null, weight 0.0 — and carries nothing; it is not needed here because the driver's dwell is one continuous in-geofence run and the POL-NS-06 limb (i) accumulation of separate intervals is not in issue. No artifact carrying a deciding fact is impaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d) (arrival marker 10 seconds from the nearest fix; 102 fixes, 100 percent coverage, no gaps; 4 chat messages matching the trip record's chat_message_count; cancellation-fee line reconciling with the resolution rule), so no POL-GEN-02(2) discount applies and confidence is 0.90."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

