    "explanation": "This case is escalated to a human reviewer, and that decision replaces any money outcome. Here is what the record shows and why.\n\nOn chargeability (for the driver): all four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold. The 'arrived' event is at 06:41:20 (EV-TRIP-00207); EV-GPS-00207 puts you inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius from the first qualifying fix at 06:41:10, with a closest approach of 14.47 m, holding still for one continuous in-geofence run of 507 seconds up to the 06:49:37 cancellation — 207 seconds beyond the 300-second STANDARD minimum — with no boarding event and cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW. None of the displacing clauses applies: this is not a wrong-entrance case (you were inside the radius, so POL-NS-03 is not engaged), there is no false arrival marker (14.47 m away and stationary at the marker, so POL-NS-05 does not bite), and there is no waiting-period shortfall (507 s against 300 s, so POL-NS-06 cannot be reached). The SGD 4.00 charged reconciles with the resolution rule — the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), which tie — so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nOn your account (for the rider): you say you came down a few minutes late, but the evidence does not support it. The rider device track in the same trace (118 fixes, 06:34:00–06:52:00) never comes closer than about 1,894 m to the pin, and the chat log EV-CHAT-00207 contains no message from you — its four messages are the system 'driver has arrived' notice and three from the driver. POL-NS-04 therefore fails at limb (a) with none of your own messages on the record, and its limb (c) is affirmatively failed on the rider's own track.\n\nOn the driver's payout (for the driver): POL-NS-07 would have paid you 80 percent of the SGD 4.00, that is SGD 3.20. But the clause's anti-farming check trips on your own profile (EV-DPROF-00207): no_show_terminations_30d is 7, at or above the threshold of 4, and 7 divided by 61 completed trips is 0.115, above 0.08. Both limbs are required and both hold, so compensation is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d).\n\nEffect: this is a terminal escalation. No monetary ruling issues and both amount fields are null. The disputed SGD 4.00 is held, not collected and not refunded, so it remains at payment_status PENDING with refund_issued_sgd 0.00. The escalation packet directs the reviewer, under POL-NS-07, to refund the rider's cancellation fee of SGD 4.00 in full. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is missing (null payload, weight 0.0); nobody relies on it, and while its absence makes POL-NS-06(i) unavailable, the summing of separate intervals is not in issue because the dwell here is a single continuous run."
