    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver: the SGD 4.00 no-show fee was correctly charged on this trip, but the platform cannot finally settle the money here. The anti-farming rule in POL-NS-07 withholds the driver's payout and sends the dispute to a human reviewer, so the SGD 4.00 is held — not refunded and not collected — until that review is done.\n\nWhat the record shows. The driver reached Blk 682 Woodlands Ave 6 and his GPS trace (EV-GPS-00207) puts him inside the 50 m STANDARD pickup radius from 06:41:10, closest fix 14.47 m, 52 qualifying in-radius fixes across a 100% covered trace with no gaps. He then held position continuously for 507 seconds to the cancellation at 06:49:37 — 207 seconds more than the 300 seconds POL-NS-01(c) requires for a STANDARD pickup — and the trip was ended by the driver with reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW and no boarding event (EV-TRIP-00207). All four limbs of POL-NS-01 therefore hold, and nothing in POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces the charge: he was inside the arrival radius, not at the wrong face of the building (POL-NS-03 not engaged); the 'arrived' marker was not false, since at 06:41:20 he was already stationary inside the geofence 14.47 m from the pin, not 300 m away or moving at 15 km/h (POL-NS-05 not engaged); and there was no waiting-period shortfall (POL-NS-06 not engaged).\n\nYour exoneration clauses do not help you, rider. POL-NS-04 fails at its first limb because EV-CHAT-00207 holds four messages and not one is yours — MSG-00207-001 is the system 'driver has arrived' notice and the other three are the driver's. It also fails at limb (c): your own device track in EV-GPS-00207 places you about 1,894 m from the pickup pin for the whole waiting window, with rider_qualifying_fix_count of 0 against the 100 m STANDARD presence radius, so your account that you 'came down, just a few minutes late' is not supported by your own device.\n\nThe amount is right. The STANDARD zone-class fee and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee are both SGD 4.00, so the GREATER under fee_schedule.resolution_rule is SGD 4.00, which is exactly the fare_breakdown cancellation-fee line — no POL-NS-08(d) integrity defect. The evidence carrying the driver's case is unimpaired under POL-NS-08(a) to (d): 10-second cadence, arrival marker 10 seconds from the nearest fix, chat count matching the trip record. EV-ADVIS-00207-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0; nobody relies on it and it is not needed, because the driver's 507-second dwell is a single continuous run, so the limb (i) accumulation it would permit is not in issue.\n\nWhy this is not a payout to the driver, and not a win for the rider either. On a verified no-show the driver's entitlement under POL-NS-07 would be SGD 3.20, being 80% of the SGD 4.00 fee. But POL-NS-07's anti-farming check fires on both limbs of the driver's own record: no_show_terminations_30d is 7, at or above the threshold of 4, and 7 divided by completed_trips_30d of 61 is 0.115, above 0.08. Both limbs are required and both hold, so compensation is withheld and the case escalates under POL-NS-09(d). That escalation is terminal: no refund and no compensation issue now, and the SGD 4.00 stays on hold at payment_status PENDING. This is not a finding of fault against the driver on this trip — his conduct here was correct — and it is not a refund to the rider; it is the platform declining to decide the money until it has reviewed the driver's 30-day termination pattern. The rider's own profile does not aggravate matters: POL-NS-09(d) reads no_show_disputes_30d, which is 1, below the trigger of 3, and the lifetime prior_no_show_flags counter is context only under POL-GEN-01 and may not be substituted for it. Confidence is 0.90, above the 0.70 floor, and rests on full-weight platform telemetry; the escalation comes from POL-NS-07 and POL-NS-09(d), not from any doubt about the facts."
